From a6164f8289804868a4a414ae7bfd3d6ab6fcaea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:13:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/39] s13d g4 cont4: right inward shift as one pinned segment

The pinned step now carries its precondition's converse, which retires the
separate precondition predicate; pinned segments bundle a contract with its
pinned step and compose by zr_segSeq. The right inward shift at level i is
one segment of thirty catalog leaves: two donor columns on scratch, the
donor's track cleared, two cuts, the donor and receiver written back, the
scratch cleared. Tape 0's endpoint is the zoned tape of the shifted track
(zr_inA3, through zr_shiftIn_tape). The extension-based donor write and its
lemmas are dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0155fKrzMUhziJHzQxJacYbw
